#
# A false positive: confirm the value is not a real credential -- compare it
# against the real .env without printing either -- and say what it is here.
# Better still, write test placeholders in a shape no rule matches (low
# entropy, e.g. "test-key"), so nothing needs pinning. PRs are squash-merged:
# a fingerprint names a commit, so one pinned on a branch commit no longer
# matches once develop holds the squashed commit; after the merge, add the
# squash commit's fingerprint in a follow-up.
#
# A real leak: the key is already public. Revoke and rotate it FIRST (the
# Hyperliquid agent key, OpenRouter, Alchemy/Infura, the deploy SSH key -- any
# of them), then pin its fingerprint here with "rotated on <YYYY-MM-DD>". Do
# not rewrite history or force-push develop: GitHub keeps PR refs and cached
# commit views reachable anyway, and every worktree would break.
